# app.Dockerfile's context (the repo root), as an allowlist: nothing but what yarn install and an app's Gradle build
# read. The checkout also holds gigabytes that must never go to Docker (a test server's data, Windows build outputs,
# test media), so everything is out unless named here.
*

# The workspace: yarn install
!package.json
!yarn.lock
!.yarnrc.yml
!.yarn/releases
!packages/*/package.json
!apps/*/package.json
!packages/build-tools/bin

# Each package's and app's sources for the Android build: its config files at the top, JS, Android, C++
!packages/*/*.js
!packages/*/*.json
!packages/*/src
!packages/*/android
!packages/*/cpp
!apps/*/*.js
!apps/*/*.json
!apps/*/src
!apps/*/android

# The libraries' build:android:docker outputs the app builds with (Turborepo makes them first)
!packages/react-native-mpv/third_party/ffmpeg/android-arm64-v8a
!packages/react-native-mpv/third_party/mpv/android-arm64-v8a
!packages/rn-trace/third_party/perfetto

# ...and within those, never local build state
**/node_modules
**/build
**/.cxx
**/.gradle
**/local.properties
